WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.017 --> 00:00:02.580
- And another thing, wait,
I have to say this though,

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.150
side note, is you, another
thing that's been going on

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.530
while you're at home is snacks, right?

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.130
You're really into pretty random snacks.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.400
- I can't stop eating.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.920
I don't know what's gotten into me.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.770
I think it's kind of being
home in the quarantine.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.790
I usually eat really
healthy when I'm on tour

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.470
and you know how this is,
I was on tour for six years

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.240
and all I was eating was like

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.000
grilled chicken breast
and rice and spinach,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.710
and sometimes green room gummy bears.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.480
But I,
(laughing)

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.590
since I've been home I've
had time to experiment

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.170
with different snacks and
I take it pretty seriously.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.120
Yeah.
- I love it.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.370
Well, maybe you can explain
some of these snacks

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.880
you've tweeted about.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.997
This one is "Dry Oreos are so weird to me.

00:00:45.997 --> 00:00:49.375
"Need dunkage," which I totally get.

00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:51.970
I have to, I like a cookie
soaked, I'm with you.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.690
I'm like, "Let's just soak
it a little bit," yep.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.770
- I can't eat 'em dry.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.910
I don't know, I don't understand
people who eat Oreos dry.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.670
They also have to be double-stuffed.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.490
That's a rule for me.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.240
And sometimes I like to
smear peanut butter on them,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.970
which is an old trick I learned

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:12.670
from watching "The Parent
Trap" when I was a young child.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.250
- Yes, oh my gosh, I love that movie.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.605
Also, I would really love your metabolism.

00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:19.560
(laughs)

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.750
Like, wait, what?

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.020
She's like, Double-stuffed."

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.090
I'm like, "Aaah," okay.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.270
What's your latest snack obsession?

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.410
- I started making Rice Krispie treats,

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.250
but without the Rice Krispies.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.370
And I know that doesn't make any sense,

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.780
but I'm make 'em with other cereals,

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.300
so like Fruity Pebble treats

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.420
or like Cinnamon Toast Crunch treats

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.953
and they're so easy to
make and they're so good.

